-- title:
--   Residual block of the rectangular GL₂ spectral expansion
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field, $\alpha,\beta$ reals with $0<\alpha$ and $\alpha<\beta$. Fix a Haar measure $\nu_{Z}$ on the idele units $(\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$ (with a Borel measurable structure) and a set $\Omega_K$ that is a fundamental domain for the image of $K^\times$ under $\nu_Z$, a finite set $S_K$ of finite places, a character $\xi_K$ of the full subgroup $\top\le(\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$ with values in $\mathbb{C}^\times$ which is continuous, unitary, and trivial on principal ideles, an ideal $N\subseteq\mathcal O_K$ all of whose prime divisors lie in $S_K$, and an archimedean type family $\mathrm{tys}_K$. Write $D=\mathtt{canonicalTruncationDomain}\,K\,\alpha\,\beta$, $\mu$ for the Haar measure $\mathtt{adelicGLHaar}$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, and let $P$ be the carrier data $\mathtt{productionPinsOf}$ with domain $D$, level groups $M\mapsto\mathtt{principalLevel}\,M\sqcap\mathtt{finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup}$, Hecke generators $\mathtt{heckeGen}$, box $\mathtt{adelicBox}\,K$, central subgroup $\top$ and the measure $\nu$ on $\mathbb{A}_K$ obtained by conditioning additive Haar measure on $\mathtt{adelicBox}\,K$. The assertion is: for every continuous compactly supported $f:\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)\to\mathbb{C}$ which is factorizable (a product of a smooth compactly supported archimedean factor and a locally constant compactly supported finite factor), bi-invariant under $\mathtt{principalLevel}\,N\sqcap\mathtt{finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup}$, and archimedeanly bi-finite of type $\mathrm{tys}_K$; for every compact $C$ and measurable $A,B\subseteq C$; and for all functions $u_c,u_r,u_e$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ each satisfying $\mathtt{IsAutomorphicFnAt}$ for $P$ and $\xi_K$, such that the constant term of $u_c$ along the unipotent $x\mapsto\binom{1\ x}{0\ 1}$ against $\nu$ vanishes $\mu$-almost everywhere, $u_r$ is approximated in $L^2(\mu|_D)$ to arbitrary accuracy by automorphic elements of the residual span (the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the functions $g\mapsto\chi(\det g)$ with $\chi^2=\xi_K$ on $\top$), $u_e$ is $L^2(\mu|_D)$-orthogonal to every automorphic $h$ that either has almost everywhere vanishing constant term or lies in the residual span, and $u_c+u_r+u_e$ agrees $\mu|_D$-almost everywhere with the automorphisation $g\mapsto\sum^{\mathrm f}_{q\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K)/Z}\int \xi_K(w)^{-1}\,\mathbf 1_{D}\mathbf 1_{B}\bigl(w\cdot(q g)\bigr)\,d\nu_Z(w)$ (central scalars $w$, global points $q$): one has $$\int_A (\mathtt{convOp}\,f\,u_r)\,d\mu|_D=\frac{\nu_Z\bigl(\Omega_K\cap\{z:\|\det(zI)\|_{\mathbb{A}}\in[\alpha,\beta]\}\bigr)}{\mu(D)}\iint_{A\times B}\sum^{\mathrm f}_{\chi}\Bigl(\int f(g)\chi(\det g)\,d\mu(g)\Bigr)\chi(\det x)\,\chi^{-1}(\det y)\,d(\mu|_D\otimes\mu|_D),$$ where $\mathtt{convOp}\,f\,u_r(g)=\int u_r(gx)f(x)\,d\mu(x)$, the idele norm is the distributive Haar character, and the finite sum runs over the continuous characters $\chi$ of $(\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$ with $\chi^2=\xi_K$ that are trivial on principal ideles.
--
--   This is the residual contribution to the rectangular (bi-measurable-set) form of the $L^2$ spectral expansion of the automorphic kernel of $f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over a number field: the residual part of the automorphised indicator of $B$ is expanded in the one-dimensional automorphic representations $\chi\circ\det$ with $\chi^2=\xi_K$, on each of which right convolution by $f$ acts by the scalar $\int f\cdot(\chi\circ\det)$. It feeds the assembly of the full expansion, where the cuspidal, residual and error blocks are combined and continued in the spectral parameter.
